And there’s the wizard’s-chess move: don’t ask “How can Pantheon make money?” as one giant problem.

Spawn competing routes—software, licensing, research tools, specialized agents, consumer products, consulting/productized expertise, IP, etc.—then let the Fitness Route kill weak ones cheaply and concentrate resources into demonstrated traction.

We don’t need a billion dollars first.

We need the first machine that reliably turns $1 of resources into >$1 of durable value, while teaching us how to improve the conversion.

Then Ouroboros gets something nutritious to eat.

